WEBVTT

00:00:03.560 --> 00:00:07.040
Without a ribber,
adding both knit and Purl stitches

00:00:07.106 --> 00:00:10.210
on a flatbed machine takes a bit of work.

00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:15.040
You need to reform individual stitches
to create ribbing

00:00:15.106 --> 00:00:17.130
and textured stitch patterns.

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:20.440
One of the first techniques that many
machine knitters learn

00:00:20.506 --> 00:00:22.930
is called mock ribbing.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:29.210
This is a hem that imitates ribbing
without it reforming any stitches.

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:32.290
If you haven't
tried this, please do.

00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:40.080
It's very quick and easy, and it's a great
technique to have in your bag of tricks.

00:00:41.720 --> 00:00:45.530
Get started by casting
on with every other needle.

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:50.490
I used an E-Wrap cast on because
it's nice and stretchy.

00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:56.650
Now make sure that the empty needles are
in out of work position and knit twice

00:00:56.720 --> 00:01:00.320
the desired length of your ribbing.

00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:06.320
Now, pick up the cast on edge and hang
the loops of your cast

00:01:06.386 --> 00:01:10.200
on into the emptied needles.

00:01:18.480 --> 00:01:21.490
When you're done,
all the needles will have stitches,

00:01:21.560 --> 00:01:25.080
and all the needles are in work.

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:34.933
Now
for our swatch here,

00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:42.040
knit a few rows or continue knitting
your garment and just bind off.

00:01:46.640 --> 00:01:52.130
The secret to nice mock
rib is in the finishing.

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:57.200
Now, once you've removed your work
from the machine, insert a pencil or ruler

00:01:57.667 --> 00:02:02.960
or a straight knitting needle
into to the hem, into the fold there,

00:02:03.026 --> 00:02:06.450
and give it a pull to set the stitches.

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:10.930
The knitting contracts
and gives the appearance of ribbing

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:14.920
without a lot of muss and fuss.

00:02:15.680 --> 00:02:20.680
Many knitters forget about this technique,
and it's quick and easy, and again,

00:02:20.746 --> 00:02:26.280
it's a nice technique to keep
in your bag of tricks.

00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:33.450
Now, some knitters will cast on with waist
yarn and ravel cord for this technique,

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:38.320
and when they're ready to hang the hem,
they pick up the first row of stitches

00:02:38.386 --> 00:02:42.440
and put them on the empty needles.

00:02:42.800 --> 00:02:46.440
Try it both ways and see
which method you prefer.

